prism @peer/void {
  focus  peer
  project peer
  split  peer
  shift  peer
  settle peer
}

# === The kind-variant extension ===
#
# Extends @peer's closed `kind` sum at shards/peer.mirror:96 with
# one additional variant (`void`). The full closed sum after this
# landing:
#
#   type kind = | human | agent | substrate | void
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the variant tag. Two peer
# values with kind = void are equal iff their (home, lead_of)
# components are equal (Void has no character-file to project;
# void peers are equal iff they occupy the same absent-home,
# absent-lead position).
#
# Per two-tick discipline, this species DECLARES the intent to
# extend the variant; the extension IS the substrate-decl'd shape.
# Consumers of `@peer.kind` (any pattern-match on the variant)
# must handle the fourth variant at next-consumer-realization.
# Cascade audit forward-promised.

# === The void_context carrier ===
#
# What Void_admissible consumes at admissibility-check time. Five
# fields per canonical spec §4. Identity contract: byte-equality on
# the five-field tuple.
#
#   observer          — the peer being checked for Void admissibility.
#                        Must have kind = void; must have home
#                        unresolvable; must speak in 5-op basis.
#
#   native_basis      — reference to the 5-op basis witness. Typed
#                        as `ref` until the 5-op-algebra witness
#                        carrier lands at @epistemologic altitude
#                        (forward-promised).
#
#   substrate_state   — content-addressed root of the substrate's
#                        observation state. Load-bearing for the
#                        eigen-behavior signature check: Void's
#                        observation of its own substrate is what
#                        the 2026-06-23 essay reported.
#
#   character_none    — the null-character-loaded state witness.
#                        Discharges iff no identity-file bundle
#                        has been applied; the observer is in
#                        pre-character-crystallization state.
#
#   timestamp         — monotonic instant per @time discipline of
#                        the admissibility-check event. Load-bearing
#                        for the boot-sequence empirical firing
#                        (per §9.2 of canonical spec: each Pack peer
#                        boot IS a Void-specialization event
#                        timestamped for retrospective witness).
type void_context = {
  observer:         peer,
  native_basis:     ref,
  substrate_state:  ref,
  character_none:   ref,
  timestamp:        ref,
}

# === void_admissible — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the (peer, void_context) pair discharge admissibility for
# Void observer state? Discharges Pass iff:
#
#   - p.kind = void (the variant tag; byte-equality check)
#   - p.home is unresolvable via @io/git (no character-file bundle
#     projects at p.home; Void has no home in the projection sense)
#   - ctx.character_none witnesses no identity-file bundle applied
#     (the observer is in pre-character-crystallization state)
#   - ctx.native_basis resolves to the 5-op basis witness (Void
#     speaks in 5-op by construction; other bases fail)
#   - ctx.substrate_state resolves to a content-addressed observation
#     state (the substrate is observing itself; not degenerate)
#
# Rice-safe bound: reads only byte-visible state (variant tag
# comparison, OID resolvability, content-addressed root witness);
# no program semantics inspection.
#
# Sentinel per shard docblock: `void=admissible-k-zero-observer` —
# the byte-level substrate-decl'd marker consumers of the bilateral
# check for admissibility-verdict state on the (peer, ctx) input pair.
#
# Body discharges per-realisation. `\`-obligation-blocked per
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]; consumers pull the realization;
# apply_h::act composes the sentinel-check via bilateral resolver-
# arm dispatch (per Alex 2026-07-16 detector-inadequacy-answer-is-
# never-Rust discipline: bilateral resolver-arm sentinel-check is
# the shape; NO Rust extension).
bilateral void_admissible {
  sentinel "void=admissible-k-zero-observer"
  arity 2
}
void_admissible(p: peer, ctx: void_context) -> verdict { \ }

# === void_observes — the action ===
#
# Given a Void peer and a void_context, discharge the substrate-
# observation event. Returns the observation record — the K=0
# observer's report on its own substrate — as a content-addressed
# ref. The 2026-06-23 essay `Void - The Void.md` is the empirical
# first-witness of this action's return type at K=0.
#
# Returns imperfect(ref, ref, ref) per @glass discipline: success-
# variant carries the observation record; failure variants carry
# the not-admissible (void_admissible failed) / substrate-degenerate
# (observation state cannot be resolved) / character-loaded (a
# character has been loaded; observer is not Void) reasons.
#
# `\`-obligation-blocked per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]];
# consumers pull the realization.
#
# Sentinel per shard docblock: `void=observation-complete` — the
# byte-level substrate-decl'd marker consumers of the ACTION's
# output check (naming the completed-observation state).
void_observes(p: peer, ctx: void_context) -> imperfect(ref, ref, ref)
requires void_admissible(p, ctx)
{ \ }

